Job Title: Security Analyst – Vulnerability Management & Audit

Department: Information Security
Reports to: Cybersecurity Manager


---

Job Summary:

The Security Analyst is responsible for conducting audit and vulnerability management activities across both CFT and DDS entities. The role involves identifying security vulnerabilities, recommending appropriate remediation measures, coordinating revalidation or retesting, and ensuring timely closure of issues. The analyst will also manage and follow up on Qualys vulnerability reports for Indian servers to maintain compliance and minimize risk exposure.


---

Key Responsibilities:

Perform audit and vulnerability assessments for CFT and DDS systems.

Review and track Qualys vulnerability scan results for Indian servers.

Provide remediation recommendations to system owners and support teams.

Conduct revalidation or retesting after remediation to ensure vulnerabilities are closed.

Collaborate with infrastructure and application teams to manage patching and mitigation activities.

Maintain detailed documentation of vulnerabilities, remediation progress, and audit reports.

Support compliance and internal/external audit requirements related to security posture.

Continuously improve vulnerability management processes and ensure timely follow-ups.



---

Qualifications:

Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or related field.

2–4 years of experience in vulnerability management, security audits, or risk assessment.

Hands-on experience with Qualys or other vulnerability management tools.

Knowledge of security controls, patch management, and remediation tracking.

Strong communication and coordination skills across technical and audit teams.



---

Key Skills:

Vulnerability Assessment & Management

Audit & Compliance

Qualys Platform (VMDR)

Remediation and Revalidation

Risk Analysis and Reporting

Cross-functional Coordination (CFT & DDS Entities)